## New experimental evidence (NEW in Round 2)

### Paper §4.6 — v9 unified-task agent on full MMAD MCQ (n=2302 QAs)
Aggregated over 9 question types: Direct 79.5% vs Agent 78.5%
(v9 does NOT systematically help MCQ over Direct). The agent wins on
Defect Description (+1.7) and Defect Classification (+1.2) but loses
on Object Classification (-3.2) and Object Details (-4.4). AD-subset
AUROC: Direct 0.759, Agent 0.723, Ens 0.776 (+1.65 pp, smaller than
the +3.03 on the older 989-item run because the v9 agent is slightly
weaker than v6 on AD). Framed in paper as an architectural
contribution, not a numerical one.

### Paper §4.7 — Per-domain active self-evolution (4 domain pilot)
With K=10 oracle queries from DEV (no test labels touched), a
DINOv2-retrieved compact neighbour prior injected into the agent's
turn-1 user message:
- D1 industrial:   0.898 → 0.971 (+7.33 pp)
- D5 brain MRI:    0.616 → 0.576 (-4.00 pp)
- D9 MVTec-LOCO:   0.602 → 0.713 (+11.11 pp)
- D12 road safety: 0.907 → 0.902 (-0.44 pp)
Mean Δ +3.5 pp, positive in 2/4 domains.

