./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:13:**Existing codebase**: Multi-round Skeptic-Verifier agent system on MMAD benchmark
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:20:The IAD field in 2025-2026 is dominated by two parallel tracks: (1) MLLM-based reasoning (optimizing MMAD accuracy via SFT+GRPO), and (2) classical unsupervised detection (PatchCore/WinCLIP variants, optimizing MVTec AUROC). Neither track addresses the **deployment gap**: after a model is deployed, it encounters unknown defect types, misses hard cases, and has no mechanism to improve from rare but valuable human annotations.
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:49:  2. Implement NRM update: after 10 human annotations, re-run detection — measure AUROC improvement on VisA bottle category
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:51:- **Expected outcome**: AAQS correlates with errors (AUC > 0.7); +2-5% AUROC after 20 annotations vs. no-feedback baseline
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:85:  - On MVTec AD, simulate AL protocol: start with 5 normal samples, add 5 per round, measure AUROC change over 5 rounds (25 total annotations)
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:88:- **Expected outcome**: Diversity strategy > uncertainty ≈ random at k=5,10,15 budget; +3-8% AUROC over static 5-shot baseline
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:109:- **Hypothesis**: Structural features of the Skeptic-Verifier's multi-round reasoning trace (debate length, consensus speed, semantic hedging tokens) are better calibrated uncertainty proxies than softmax confidence for IAD queries, enabling a more efficient active learning query strategy.
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:117:  - Run existing Skeptic-Verifier on 200 MMAD samples
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:163:- **Hypothesis**: Establishing a standardized active learning evaluation protocol (fixed budget sizes, oracle simulation, evaluation metrics) reveals significant performance differences between query strategies and enables reproducible AL research in visual IAD.
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:166:  - Define AL simulation protocol: start with 0 labeled defects, sequentially query oracle (ground truth labels), measure AUROC/F1 as function of annotation budget (0, 5, 10, 20, 50 labels)
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:199:**Command**: Run existing Skeptic-Verifier on MMAD subset (200 samples), extract trace features, compute error prediction AUC.
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:209:- **Success metric**: Diversity strategy AUROC > random strategy at k=10 budget
./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:222:1. **Run Pilot 1 (DebateScore)** — no code changes needed; run existing system on MMAD, analyze logs. ~1 hour.
