./review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.v8.md:146:2. **Agent score** ($s_{\mathrm{agent}}$): a per-item ReAct loop with a 13-tool library (expert probes, visual inspection, reference understanding, structural, semantic) over $K{=}5$ turns. v6 uses free-form deliberation; v8 enforces a three-phase "refutation" protocol (candidate features → refutation tool → remaining candidates → score).
./review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.v8.md:147:3. **Ensemble**: $s_{\mathrm{final}} = 0.5\!\cdot\!s_{\mathrm{Direct}} + 0.5\!\cdot\!s_{\mathrm{agent}}$ (for v6) or $0.6\!\cdot\!s_{\mathrm{Direct}} + 0.4\!\cdot\!s_{\mathrm{agent}}$ (for v8), with the weight frozen on dev.
./review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.v8.md:153:1. **Primary**: On Qwen3.5-VL-27B test ($n{=}1418$, 12 domains), $0.5\!\cdot\!\mathrm{Direct} + 0.5\!\cdot\!\mathrm{v6\_agent}$ reaches macro AUROC 0.8136, beating Direct-only (0.7684) by +4.53 pp (95% CI [+2.82, +6.31], $P(\Delta>0){=}1.000$). Matches SubspaceAD fusion on Qwen3.5 (±0), edges it on GPT-5.4 (+0.87 pp).
./review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.v8.md:155:3. **Interpretable variant**: v8 refutation agent gains +1.28 pp on Qwen3.5 test (CI touches zero, one-sided $P{=}0.962$); provides auditable per-item trace.
