./AnomaClaw/LITERATURE_SURVEY.md:4:**Topic**: MLLM-based universal visual anomaly detection agent + active learning
./AnomaClaw/LITERATURE_SURVEY.md:12:1. **MLLM-based Industrial AD** (crowded): Fine-tuning or prompting MLLMs for industrial defect detection on MMAD/MVTec. Dominated by GRPO/SFT approaches (AnomalyR1, OmniAD, EMIT). AgentIAD claims 97.62% on MMAD but is essentially tool-augmented single-model inference, not a genuine agentic system.
./AnomaClaw/LITERATURE_SURVEY.md:24:| Paper | Venue | Method | MMAD Acc | Notes |
./AnomaClaw/LITERATURE_SURVEY.md:27:| MMAD Benchmark | ICLR 2025 | Evaluation protocol | GPT-4o: 74.9% | Benchmark, not method |
./AnomaClaw/LITERATURE_SURVEY.md:75:The intersection of (1) training-free cross-domain AD, (2) genuine agent-based reasoning, and (3) human-in-the-loop active learning is completely unoccupied. A universal AD agent tested across 8+ domains with GPT/SeedVL backends would be the first of its kind. If existing benchmarks are too large, a carefully sampled cross-domain benchmark would itself be a contribution.
