./archive/old_docs/EXPERIMENT_SUMMARY_20260412.md:102:**Key insight**: Agent helps weaker backbones significantly (SeedVL +2.9pp, 9/11 domains improved) but ties the strongest backbone (GPT-5.4). The dominant contribution remains the descriptor fix (+7.1pp).
./archive/old_docs/EXPERIMENT_SUMMARY_20260412.md:104:**Experiment audit**: PASSED — no data leakage, thresholds from calibration only, AUROC numbers verified.
./archive/old_docs/EXPERIMENT_SUMMARY_20260412.md:108:| Variant | Architecture | GPT-5.4 test macro | SeedVL test macro | vs v0 (GPT) |
./archive/old_docs/EXPERIMENT_SUMMARY_20260412.md:117:**Conclusion**: Agent v1 (simple agree/disagree + VLM interpret on disagreement) is the most robust variant. It matches v0 on GPT-5.4 and improves SeedVL by +2.9pp. More aggressive routing (v2, v3) overfits calibration thresholds.
