./archive/old_docs/PAPER_PLAN.md:4:**One-sentence contribution**: AnomalyClaw is a training-free agent that adaptively combines VLM single-pass reasoning with non-parametric patch-level expert evidence through a disagreement-triggered interpret mechanism, achieving +2.9pp macro AUROC over single-pass VLM on an 11-domain cross-domain benchmark while demonstrating that task-anchored domain descriptors alone provide the dominant +7.1pp improvement.
./archive/old_docs/PAPER_PLAN.md:16:| C2: AnomalyClaw improves non-frontier VLMs | SeedVL +2.9pp (9/11 domains); GPT tie | Fully supported | §4.2 |
./archive/old_docs/PAPER_PLAN.md:27:- **Result**: SeedVL +2.9pp, GPT tie; descriptors alone +7.1pp
./archive/old_docs/PAPER_PLAN.md:35:- **Key citations**: MMAD, AgentIAD, EAGLE, PatchCore, WinCLIP, SubspaceAD
./archive/old_docs/PAPER_PLAN.md:39:- VLM-based AD (AnomalyGPT, MMAD)
./archive/old_docs/PAPER_PLAN.md:55:- §4.3 Per-domain analysis (Table 3: SeedVL breakdown)
