./paper/figures/gen_bootstrap_cis.py:38:    "SeedVL":   "seedvl_agent_v1_test.json",
./paper/figures/gen_bootstrap_cis.py:194:    # We do not have per-item generic scores for SeedVL/Qwen, so we note it as
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:16:The agent must beat **direct VLM (v0)** — i.e. the no-agent baseline that just calls the VLM with the descriptor — by **≥ 5 pp macro AUROC** on the test split, on at least one backbone (Qwen3.5 first), then on GPT-5.4 and SeedVL.
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:19:- SeedVL direct = 0.779 → target ≥ 0.829
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:22:Score fusion (`0.8·s_v0 + 0.2·σ(s_exp)`) already beats direct on all three backbones (Qwen3.5 +5.5 pp, SeedVL +1.7 pp, GPT-5.4 +1.5 pp), so the simplest agent (apply per-domain fusion when expert is reliable, direct otherwise) should comfortably clear +5 pp on Qwen3.5 and meet or approach it on SeedVL/GPT-5.4.
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:108:2. Run on Qwen3.5 calibration (220 items, fast). Confirm calibration macro AUROC ≥ fusion + 4 pp.
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:110:4. If yes → port to SeedVL test, then GPT-5.4 (limited budget).
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:117:- Do not introduce per-image VLM router calls that add cost without proven AUROC gain.
./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:119:- Do not claim AUROC numbers without paired bootstrap CIs against fusion.
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:12:- Computed per-(backbone, strategy, domain) AUROC on test.
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:16:**Key finding**: Per-domain oracle strategy varies significantly across the 12 domain codes. Oracle macro AUROC vs best-single-strategy:
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:18:- SeedVL: oracle 0.825 vs fusion 0.796 → +2.9 pp
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:33:**Macro AUROC (test, 1418 items, D8 fallback = direct for fusion):**
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:34:| | GPT-5.4 | SeedVL | Qwen3.5 |
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:53:| **SeedVL** | **calibration-router vs fusion** | **+0.016** | **[+0.000, +0.032]** | **✓** |
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:54:| SeedVL | descriptor-router vs direct | +0.022 | [+0.014, +0.031] | ✓ |
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:55:| SeedVL | oracle vs calibration-router | +0.013 | [+0.001, +0.025] | ✓ |
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:61:- `figures/fig_intuition.pdf` — three-panel: (a) strategy heatmap per domain, (b) macro AUROC bars for direct/fusion/descriptor/calib/oracle across 3 backbones, (c) strategy mix bars (oracle vs calibration).
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:63:- `figures/fig_per_domain.pdf` — per-domain strategy AUROCs with calibration router's choice overlaid per cell.
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:81:- `refine-logs/PER_DOMAIN_STRATEGY_MATRIX.{json,md}` — per-domain × strategy × backbone AUROC
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:82:- `refine-logs/ROUTER_RESULTS.json` — router assignments and macro AUROC per backbone
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:87:- `refine-logs/aggregate_strategy_matrix.py` — per-domain AUROC aggregation
./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:93:- The paper uses v1 AnomalyClaw numbers in the per-domain SeedVL table (Table 7 in Appendix); the calibration-router v2 per-domain numbers are reflected in the new Figure `fig_per_domain.pdf` and main Table 1.
./benchmark/results/active_learning/al_qwen35_D12.json:1:{"domain": "D12", "k": 10, "fewshot_k": 3, "selection": "uncertainty", "oracle_items": [{"item_id": "D12_0042", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/b747a85e-9e012bdf.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.15, "rationale": "The query image depicts a standard urban driving scene. While a large bus is present on the left, this is a normal object in the domain of city driving and not a defect or anomaly. The visual content is consistent with the general theme of the reference images (driving scenes), differing only in specific traffic and time of day, which are expected variations.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0034", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/b3853f81-272f6c37.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.88, "rationale": "The query image contains a prominent large green billboard and a specific storefront that are not present in any of the reference images, indicating a significant visual difference and thus an anomaly.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0060", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/b39fe3cd-553d15a3.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.88, "rationale": "The query image contains a prominent, large green rectangular light or reflection in the upper-left area that is not present in any of the reference images, indicating a clear anomaly.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0075", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/c6d086e9-0a3f83a3.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.1, "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirmed that the dashboard features in the query image are consistent with the reference images, refuting the initial candidate feature. No other anomalies were detected.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0020", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/c0a66d6a-607213d1.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.1, "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirmed that the visual features in the query image, specifically the road markings and texture, are consistent with the normal reference images. No anomalous features were detected.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0045", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/c02ee64a-3178b7fa.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.1, "rationale": "The query image shows a standard urban driving scene. Comparison with reference images confirms that all observed features, such as vehicles and road conditions, fall within the range of normal variation. No anomalies were detected.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0077", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/b81771ca-32f6b949.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.1, "rationale": "The query image depicts a standard night-time highway scene. The side-by-side comparison confirmed that the observed features, such as the overhead signs, are consistent with normal variations and do not indicate an anomaly.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0025", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/b6f77fda-46184a8c.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.1, "rationale": "The query image shows a typical street scene with vehicles and road conditions consistent with the normal reference images. No anomalous features were identified after refutation.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0032", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/c0697e71-84867efa.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.1, "rationale": "The query image depicts a standard daytime driving scene. Comparison with reference images (mostly night scenes) shows that the objects and scene structure are consistent with normal variations, with no unique anomalies detected.", "error": null}, {"item_id": "D12_0078", "query_path": "/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/data/BDD100K_normal/data/b996d83b-2f6ef415.jpg", "label": 0, "score": 0.08, "rationale": "The visual features in the query image, specific