./archive/paper-v0-cal-tuned/sections/0_abstract.tex:2:We present \textsc{AnomalyClaw}, a training-free framework that detects anomalies through \emph{adversarial debate} between two VLM-based agents---an Anomaly Proposer that actively searches for defects and a Normality Advocate that challenges each claim with counter-evidence---grounded by an extensible pool of lightweight vision experts.
./archive/paper-v0-cal-tuned/sections/0_abstract.tex:6:AnomalyClaw achieves \tbd{X.XXX} macro-averaged AUROC, improving over single-pass VLM baselines (\tbd{X.XXX}) and prior agent-based methods (\tbd{X.XXX}).
./archive/paper-v0-cal-tuned/sections/0_abstract.tex:7:Ablations confirm that adversarial debate outperforms single-agent reasoning by \tbd{+X.X} AUROC points, and that expert grounding contributes an additional \tbd{+X.X} points.
