./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3776:- [benchmark/scripts/compose_ensemble.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/compose_ensemble.py:38): ensemble fallback only handles missing scores, not errored records. Agent JSON failures still carry `anomaly_score=0.5`, so `compose_ensemble.py` averages Direct with synthetic 0.5 instead of falling back to Direct. In current Qwen v6.5+D this changes 6 items and slightly changes macro AUROC.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3779:- [benchmark/scripts/eval_v6.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/eval_v6.py:139): permutation logic is correct. It swaps per-item A/B scores, not labels, then recomputes macro AUROC. No core math bug found there. Minor fix: report `(count+1)/(n_perm+1)` to avoid zero p-values and disclose method-selection multiplicity.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3786:- [benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py:92), [benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py:102): expert percentile rank is computed against the whole active split. On `split="test"`, that is a transductive use of the full test score distribution. It is label-free, but not a per-item online agent.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3787:  Exact fix: compute percentile ranks against calibration/train expert-score distributions, while looking up only the current item’s raw expert score from the active split.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3824:3. Fix and use the retrieval tool as a pure visual reference augmenter: clean train-only normal bank, return retrieved images to the VLM, and test whether better references improve agent-alone AUROC without score averaging.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3842:- [benchmark/scripts/compose_ensemble.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/compose_ensemble.py:38): ensemble fallback only handles missing scores, not errored records. Agent JSON failures still carry `anomaly_score=0.5`, so `compose_ensemble.py` averages Direct with synthetic 0.5 instead of falling back to Direct. In current Qwen v6.5+D this changes 6 items and slightly changes macro AUROC.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3845:- [benchmark/scripts/eval_v6.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/eval_v6.py:139): permutation logic is correct. It swaps per-item A/B scores, not labels, then recomputes macro AUROC. No core math bug found there. Minor fix: report `(count+1)/(n_perm+1)` to avoid zero p-values and disclose method-selection multiplicity.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3852:- [benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py:92), [benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py](/hdd1/jiangxi/AD-Agent/benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v6.py:102): expert percentile rank is computed against the whole active split. On `split="test"`, that is a transductive use of the full test score distribution. It is label-free, but not a per-item online agent.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3853:  Exact fix: compute percentile ranks against calibration/train expert-score distributions, while looking up only the current item’s raw expert score from the active split.
./refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18.md:3890:3. Fix and use the retrieval tool as a pure visual reference augmenter: clean train-only normal bank, return retrieved images to the VLM, and test whether better references improve agent-alone AUROC without score averaging.
