./archive/paper-backup-20260406-165239/sections/2_related_work.tex:15:The MMAD benchmark~\cite{jiang2024mmad} formalized VLM-based anomaly detection as a visual question answering task, revealing that even state-of-the-art VLMs struggle with fine-grained defect recognition.
./archive/paper-backup-20260406-165239/sections/2_related_work.tex:16:AD-Copilot~\cite{zhang2026adcopilot} proposed an interactive assistant paradigm where a VLM guides users through the anomaly detection workflow.
./archive/paper-backup-20260406-165239/sections/2_related_work.tex:62:MMAD~\cite{jiang2024mmad} covers industrial defect detection across MVTec-AD and VisA categories but does not extend beyond manufactured objects and textures.
