./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:1363:        "evidence": "The query image has a significantly higher density of larger, elongated dark inclusions across the entire surface, which differs consistently from the sparse, small scattered inclusions seen in all normal reference examples.",
./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:1395:        "evidence": "The query image displays a typical fine-speckled concrete texture consistent with normal infrastructure surface patterns, no significant abnormal features are present.",
./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:1449:        "evidence": "The query image displays a natural speckled stone texture consistent with the range of normal concrete/stone surface variations shown in the references, with no significant abnormal features present.",
./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:2005:        "evidence": "Compared to the reference benign moles, the query lesion has irregular borders, asymmetric shape, significant uneven color variation with multiple dark concentrated pigmented regions, all features consistent with malignant melanoma.",
./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:2229:        "evidence": "Compared to the benign nevi (normal references), the query lesion has irregular, asymmetric shape, irregular blurred borders, and significant heterogeneous color variation, which matches features of malignant melanoma.",
./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:2261:        "evidence": "The query lesion exhibits significant asymmetry, irregular border, and prominent color variation (mixed lighter hypopigmented areas and uneven dark/red-brown pigment distribution), features consistent with malignant melanoma, which is abnormal compared to the reference benign melanocytic nevi.",
./benchmark/results/factorial/seed2_v0_k4_calib.json:2357:        "evidence": "Compared to the benign normal reference moles, the query lesion has irregular asymmetric shape, uneven irregular borders, and significant mixed color variation (heterogeneous pigmentation with pink and varying shades of red/brown), which matches the features of malignant melanoma.",
