./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:1325:            "reasoning": "The queried finding is a smooth, pink, moist mucosal prominence with strong specular reflection and no clear ulceration, irregular surface, active bleeding, necrosis, or distinct demarcated mass. Its appearance is consistent with normal endoscopic fold/lumen contour variation seen in the references, where the lumen can appear narrowed or slit-like and mucosal folds can form rounded bulges depending on viewing angle and distension. The focal narrowing is therefore explainable by normal fold-dominated anatomy rather than a true abnormal lesion."
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:3753:            "reasoning": "The queried area shows overall smooth, glossy pink mucosa with normal folds/rugae and a patent recessed lumen, matching the normal patterns in the references. The tiny reddish pinpoint/short faint marks on the right-lower wall are very subtle, without a clear mucosal break, crater, adherent exudate, active bleeding, or definite irregular ulcer/erosion. Their appearance can be explained by normal mucosal color variation, mild focal erythema, viewing angle, or slight contact/pressure effect from the scope rather than a true pathologic lesion."
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:5722:            "reasoning": "The overall orange-red coloration and mildly uneven texture remain within the normal range of mucosal color and fold-related surface variation shown across the references. The mucosa is still smooth, moist, and glossy without a focal destructive lesion, exudate, active bleeding, or irregular mass. This is best explained by benign color-tone variation and close-up viewing angle."
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:5936:            "pattern": "No obvious large protruding mass, deep ulcer crater, or active bleeding is visible in these normal examples.",
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:9333:            "reasoning": "There is focal fresh red hemorrhagic change immediately adjacent to the protruding lesion, with visible active-looking blood/redness not seen in the reference normals. This is more than mild normal color variation and is not explained by specular highlights, mucus, or folds. It is a genuine abnormal bleeding/inflamed area."
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:16560:            "pattern": "No obvious large exophytic mass, deep crater, or active bleeding is visible in these normal references.",
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5d.json:2696:            "benign_explanation": "This appears to be a difference in scope angle, distension, and normal mucosal folding rather than a discrete lesion. No ulcer, mass, active bleeding, erosion, or clear mucosal defect is visible. Under the fp_benign_variation rule, fold prominence/asymmetry alone is insufficient.",
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5d.json:4387:            "benign_explanation": "This appearance is well explained by transient endoscope contact/pressure and viewing angle. Similar instrument-associated deformation is seen in reference 2, and there is no clear ulcer, mass, active bleeding, or focal destructive lesion.",
./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D1.json:382:            "benign_explanation": "The mark is very shallow, low-contrast, and consistent with minor fabric weave variation, pressure mark, or lighting/shadow change. No tearing, snagging, broken zipper teeth, staining, or structurally significant damage is visible. Given the scout failure mode fp_benign_variation, this does not provide strong positive defect evidence.",
