review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1951:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:41:  tool_reference_profiler()
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1952:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:54:  tool_domain_knowledge(question)
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1953:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:55:    Targeted text question to an LLM. May hallucinate; cross-check.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1954:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:63:  1. `detection`:    refs present, no question.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1955:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:64:     → refutation protocol; output anomaly_score.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1956:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:65:  2. `mcq_binary`:   refs + question + options like A/B (Yes/No).
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1957:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:66:     → refutation protocol; output anomaly_score AND mcq_answer.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1958:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:67:  3. `mcq_choice`:   question + 4 options A/B/C/D (defect type,
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1959:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:68:                     location, object class, etc.).
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1960:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:69:     → observe + match evidence to options; output mcq_answer.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:1961:benchmark/scripts/agent_prompt_v9.py:70:  4. `open_ended`:   question, no options.
