review-stage/codex_review_r3_raw.out:1853:review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1734:The ablation numbers in the log match the script, but I’m seeing a methodological issue: the v6-BIN transform is described as rank-preserving, while the implementation median-splits to two constants, creating many ties and dropping standalone AUROC from 0.7713 to 0.6928. That means this ablation currently mixes “loss of middle mass” with “loss of within-half rank information.”
