review-stage/codex_review_r3_raw.out:6190:review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2387:paper/sections/0_abstract.tex:3:\textbf{Main finding.} On \textbf{CrossDomainVAD-11} (12 domains, $1{,}418$ test items), a simple arithmetic ensemble of the VLM's Direct score and a tool-using ReAct agent's score reaches macro AUROC $0.8136$ on Qwen3.5-VL-27B, beating the descriptor-only Direct VLM baseline $0.7684$ by $+4.53$ pp (stratified paired bootstrap 95\% CI $[+2.82, +6.31]$, $P(\Delta\!>\!0){=}1.000$). The ensemble recipe is $s_{\mathrm{final}} = 0.5\!\cdot\!s_{\mathrm{Direct}} + 0.5\!\cdot\!s_{\mathrm{agent}}$, \emph{frozen} on dev before any test query is seen. The recipe beats the stronger SubspaceAD \emph{fusion} baseline by $+0.9$ pp on GPT-5.4 and matches it on Qwen3.5, using only VLM outputs, no additional expert model.
review-stage/codex_review_r3_raw.out:6202:review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:59:Key claim: "a simple 0.5·Direct + 0.5·v6-agent ensemble reaches macro AUROC 0.8136, beating the descriptor-only Direct VLM baseline (0.7684) by +4.52 pp (stratified paired bootstrap 95% CI [+2.82, +6.31], P(Δ>0)=1.000 on 1,418 items)."
review-stage/codex_review_r3_raw.out:6203:review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:448:test** (0.7684 → 0.8136, 12-domain macro AUROC, n=1418). The V8
review-stage/codex_review_r3_raw.out:6207:review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:789:On our \textbf{CrossDomainVAD-11} benchmark (12 domains, $1{,}418$ test items, Qwen3.5-VL-27B backbone), a simple $0.5\!\cdot\!\mathrm{Direct} + 0.5\!\cdot\!\mathrm{v6.5\text{-}agent}$ ensemble reaches macro AUROC $0.8136$, beating the descriptor-only Direct VLM baseline ($0.7684$) by \textbf{$+4.52$ pp} (stratified paired bootstrap 95\% CI $[+2.82, +6.31]$, $P(\Delta>0){=}1.000$ on $1{,}418$ items). The refutation agent (v8) ensembled with Direct reaches $0.7812$ ($+1.28$ pp) and provides interpretable traces; a triple blend $0.5\!\cdot\!\mathrm{Direct} + 0.1\!\cdot\!\mathrm{v6.5\text{-}agent} + 0.4\!\cdot\!\mathrm{v8}$ sits in between at $0.8036$ ($+3.52$ pp). On GPT-5.4 dev the same recipe generalises: the best triple blend over Direct, v6.6 self-ensemble, and v8 gives $+2.4$ pp (n=480). We localise the source of ensemble gain with score-distribution histograms: the $+4.5$ pp effect correlates with the agent's middle-zone mass ($24$\% for v6.5 vs $0.4$\% for v8), not with the agent's stand-alone accuracy.
