review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:900:./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:13:**Existing codebase**: Multi-round Skeptic-Verifier agent system on MMAD benchmark
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:901:./AnomaClaw/IDEA_REPORT.md:20:The IAD field in 2025-2026 is dominated by two parallel tracks: (1) MLLM-based reasoning (optimizing MMAD accuracy via SFT+GRPO), and (2) classical unsupervised detection (PatchCore/WinCLIP variants, optimizing MVTec AUROC). Neither track addresses the **deployment gap**: after a model is deployed, it encounters unknown defect types, misses hard cases, and has no mechanism to improve from rare but valuable human annotations.
