review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1764:./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:16:The agent must beat **direct VLM (v0)** — i.e. the no-agent baseline that just calls the VLM with the descriptor — by **≥ 5 pp macro AUROC** on the test split, on at least one backbone (Qwen3.5 first), then on GPT-5.4 and SeedVL.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1767:./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:108:2. Run on Qwen3.5 calibration (220 items, fast). Confirm calibration macro AUROC ≥ fusion + 4 pp.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1769:./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:117:- Do not introduce per-image VLM router calls that add cost without proven AUROC gain.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1770:./refine-logs/RESEARCH_IDEA.md:119:- Do not claim AUROC numbers without paired bootstrap CIs against fusion.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1771:./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:12:- Computed per-(backbone, strategy, domain) AUROC on test.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1772:./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:16:**Key finding**: Per-domain oracle strategy varies significantly across the 12 domain codes. Oracle macro AUROC vs best-single-strategy:
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1774:./refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_LOG_20260415.md:33:**Macro AUROC (test, 1418 items, D8 fallback = direct for fusion):**
