review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6244:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:2387:            "description": "Query shows a curbside parked-car row immediately along the right-side sidewalk, with the camera vehicle positioned close behind a parked wagon/sedan rather than centered in an active travel lane as in the references.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6245:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:2802:            "description": "There are very few active traffic participants ahead, with mostly parked vehicles on the right and an empty lane, whereas the references show normal traffic flow or parked-car frontage in more populated settings.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6246:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:3216:            "positive_evidence": "The query contains multiple active vehicles with bright headlights spread across the left-center and center near the intersection area, suggesting crossing/oncoming traffic. The references are dominated by parked roadside vehicles and only sparse forward traffic, with no comparable cluster of active cross-traffic.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6247:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:3217:            "benign_explanation": "Traffic density can fluctuate by time and location, so vehicle count alone is somewhat variable; however, the arrangement at an active intersection is notably different from the reference scenes.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6248:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:3829:            "description": "Oncoming headlights from opposing traffic are visible on the left side of the query, indicating active opposing traffic in a two-way street; this pattern is absent or not similarly prominent in the references.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6249:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:3930:            "description": "Roadway appears wider with several active lanes in the same direction, whereas the references mostly show narrower or simpler lane layouts.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6250:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:4432:            "description": "Traffic lights are visibly green ahead over the intersection; several reference images either show no active signal in view or different roadway states, making the signalized open-intersection state a deviation candidate.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6251:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:4747:            "description": "Visible green overhead traffic signal controlling the lane approach, whereas the references do not show an equivalent active signalized intersection scene.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6252:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:5776:            "description": "The setting is a wooded parking area with no surrounding traffic, unlike the reference images that show active urban/suburban road scenes with multiple vehicles on streets.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6253:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D7.json:5853:            "description": "The scene is a curbside parade/town-street style setting with buildings and spectators, not a forward-facing lane-view of active driving on urban roads/highways as in the references.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6254:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj2_k4_test_D7.json:1756:            "reasoning": "The object slightly right of center appears to be a normal roadside fixture placed on a small pedestrian refuge/curb extension at the far side of the crosswalk, not standing in an active travel lane. This fits normal urban street infrastructure and roadway-guidance elements already covered by the normality profile. It does not indicate an unusual or hazardous scene anomaly."
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6255:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj2_k4_test_D7.json:5167:            "pattern": "Other vehicles are present ahead or alongside, indicating active city traffic.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6399:./benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5.json:7774:            "description": "Localized erythematous/pink reactive-looking zone surrounding and extending beyond the pigmented core.",
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6402:The paper already contains the Round 2 edits in §4: SeedVL is explicitly non-significant, v9 is framed as not improving full MCQ, and AL is described as exploratory. Now I’m moving from text to recomputation from JSON, which is where hidden problems usually show up.
