review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6515:  ✓ Audit v8/v9/active-learning implementations against paper claims
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6532:- The MMAD AUROC table is numerically wrong because MMAD labels are derived incorrectly. `benchmark/scripts/mmad_eval.py:70-71` and `benchmark/scripts/mmad_eval_v9.py:69-70` use `"good" in key.lower()`, which makes every `GoodsAD/...` item normal because the dataset name contains “Good”. The paper says GoodsAD has one label class and omits AUROC (`paper/sections/4_experiments.tex:188`), but option-derived labels in the same MMAD file give GoodsAD `180` anomalous / `167` normal. Recomputing AUROC from correct answer/options gives pooled Direct/Agent/Ensemble `0.781/0.744/0.811`, not the paper’s `0.708/0.670/0.731`.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6533:- The reported MMAD MCQ regression is honest in direction: `direct_answer` is `657/989 = 66.4%`, `ensemble_answer` is `649/989 = 65.6%`, so `-0.8pp` is real. But the paper’s wording “A=Yes/B=No” and “score>0.5 -> A” at `paper/sections/4_experiments.tex:168,188` is false; the code uses option-aware mapping.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6537:- Tool/cost claims are false. The paper says tools are zero-VLM-call (`paper/sections/3_method.tex:17,23`) and at most two VLM calls (`3_method.tex:110`), but `tool_reference_profiler` calls the VLM at `benchmark/scripts/agent_tools_v7.py:412-436`, and `tool_domain_knowledge` calls an LLM at `agent_tools_v7.py:631-647`. v8/v9 also run up to 5 cognitive turns.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6541:1. **MMAD label bug invalidates the cross-benchmark AUROC numbers.**  
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6542:   Minimum fix: derive AD labels from MMAD `Options` + `Answer`, or from an official MMAD label field, not path substring. Rerun `mmad_anomaly_qwen3.json`, update GoodsAD AUROC, update pooled AUROC/CIs, and patch v9 before any per-class threshold calibration.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6559:6. **Specific concerns about the v9/AL direction**
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6561:- v9 will not automatically close the MMAD MCQ gap via rank granularity. Rank granularity explains AUROC/ranking, not thresholded MCQ accuracy or non-AD option selection. Per-class thresholds may improve AD accuracy, but that is calibration, not a unified-agent mechanism.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6562:- v9 currently inherits the MMAD label bug, so any per-class threshold calibration on GoodsAD is invalid until `mmad_eval_v9.py:69-70` is fixed.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6563:- Current v9 evidence is tiny and still moving. I observed `mmad_v9_dev500.json` at `90` QA items: Direct `47/60` earlier, then `70/90`-scale partial as the file grew; this is sanity evidence only, not a paper result.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6564:- `v9_agent_run` passes `domain_code = class_name` (`mmad_eval_v9.py:208-213`), but `tool_reference_retriever` expects CrossDomainVAD domain-code indexes. Retrieval tools likely fail or silently underperform on MMAD unless class-level indexes are built.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6566:- AL implementation is weaker than the spec: selection is only `abs(score-0.5)` (`active_learning.py:177`), not disagreement/confidence-weighted; few-shot context injects labels/rationales as text (`agent_v9.py:61-74`), not images.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:6570:Track these into Round 2: MMAD AUROC label bug; GoodsAD false single-class claim; SeedVL Direct provenance mismatch; v8 reported JSON lacks history despite auditability claims; tool/call-budget undercount; stale appendix fusion numbers; v9 threshold calibration invalid until label derivation is fixed; AL code is dev-oracle adaptation, not the test-oracle protocol in the spec.
