docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:10:of human-labelled (or oracle-GT in experiments) examples and use that
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:13:Mechanism: active selection of confusing items, GT query, inject retrieved
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:14:neighbors as few-shot evidence in the agent's system prompt.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:18:- **Benchmark**: CrossDomainVAD-11 (12 domains, 1418 test items) — primary.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:19:- **Budget**: K=10 oracle queries per domain (realistic human labelling
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:25:This is a **dev-oracle semi-supervised domain-adaptation** protocol — the
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:26:oracle pool comes from the \emph{dev} split (not test), so it is
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:27:structurally impossible for oracle labels to leak into the test AUROC.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:29:1. **Passive pass** (no oracle):
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:30:   - Run agent v9 on all test items of D. Collect
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:31:     (image, score, rationale, confidence).
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:33:   - Run agent v9 on all dev items of D first to obtain dev scores.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:38:   - Pick top-$K{=}10$ most confusing dev items.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:41:     \{0,1\}$ from the manifest. No test labels touched.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:42:4. **Build per-domain RAG** using the labelled dev items:
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:43:   - Key: DINOv2 CLS embedding of the query image.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:44:   - Value: (image path, label, agent's rationale at the time of query).
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:46:   - For each test item in D, retrieve top-$3$ nearest DEV neighbours by
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:47:     DINOv2 cosine similarity and inject them as text lines into the
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:50:     similarity=… — \<rationale\>''. (Future work: pass the neighbour
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:51:     images too; the current MVP uses text-only neighbours.)
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:53:6. **Evaluation**: per-domain AUROC on the full test split,
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:54:   \emph{pre} vs \emph{post} active pass. Oracle pool is dev (disjoint
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:55:   from test) so this is not active-learning-with-test-holdout; the right
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:68:  "rationale_initial": "agent's pre-oracle rationale",
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-19-active-learning-design.md:69:  "rationale_corrected": "rewrite after oracle correction (optional)"
