paper/sections/3_method.tex:47:    \item[\textbf{direct}.] One VLM call with the task-anchored descriptor and the first $k$ reference images. Cost: 1 VLM call.
paper/sections/3_method.tex:58:The plan is computed once per (backbone, domain) pair and frozen before any test query. At inference time the agent looks up $\pi(d)$ and executes the strategy; no per-image router call is made. The final cost is the strategy's cost for that domain (Table~\ref{tab:main_results} reports an average of $0.92$ VLM calls/image on Qwen3.5).
